# Mission Control

{{OWNER}}'s Mission Control folder. Open Claude Code here and say "set me up". It connects Claude Code
on this laptop, finds the projects you're working on, and writes a short summary of each into
`projects/`.

After that, every Claude Code session in one of those projects is timed, starts with Mission Control's
rules, and keeps its summary up to date. Come back here to ask "what needs me?", to send a project a
task, or to see your hours.

| Path | What |
|---|---|
| `CLAUDE.md` | Makes Claude your Mission Control agent in this folder |
| `projects/<id>/PROJECT.md` | One summary per project, naming the project's folder |
| `bin/mc` | The Mission Control command (runs the engine in `{{ENGINE}}`) |

Settings live in `~/.mission-control/config.json`, outside this folder, because they hold your key.
See them with `bin/mc config`.
